From 5465883f4607d41ad76fac772175d50933f3cf1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiro836 <17294277+Shiro836@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:12:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] media: per-codec real-GPU decode tests, guest
 ByteBuffer smoke, measured seccomp policy, gate decode case

real_vp9_test.cpp becomes test/real_codec_test.cpp: H.264/HEVC (Annex-B access units) and
VP9/AV1 (IVF units) through nvc2::Decoder on the real nv_video backend, NV12, P010 and the
Codec2 component's planar YV12 target, byte-compared with an FFmpeg software decode; every
unit returned once, EOS last. `make test` stays fast; realtest / realtest-all (ffmpeg-
generated streams, 9 cases) / smoke (committed 320x180 streams with pinned hashes) are
opt-in. EOS is submitted as its own empty unit, as the Codec2 front does; an EOS flag on the
last data unit is measurable with REAL_EOS_ON_LAST=1 (HEVC produced 3 wrong tail pictures
through that path on the public ABI 1 backend, correct via the separate unit).

ByteBuffer/YV12 coverage: the YV12 pool reproduces Component::Pool's target exactly
(Y stride ALIGN(width,16), Cr then Cb, NV_VIDEO_FORMAT_YUV420P) for H.264, HEVC and VP9, and
test/c2_smoke.cpp decodes MP4s through the public MediaCodec NDK on the live Codec2 service
(ByteBuffer output, CPU_READ gralloc path): H.264, HEVC, VP9, AV1 all 8/8 frames.

Seccomp policy re-measured on bionic in the guest (strace -f -c on the service while decoding
all four codecs): 25 syscalls used, none missing; 32-bit-only names and duplicates removed.
Verified by restarting the service with the edited policy bind-mounted: all four codecs decode,
no SIGSYS.

Media gate: dev/source-native run_media_gate and release_gate media_case run `make smoke` with
the advertised codec list after the caps check; the vendor-image path records that it cannot
decode (no host backend) and points at the developer gate.

Verified on the host (RTX 5090, 615.78.08, public ABI 1 backend build):
- realtest-all: 9/9 PASS (H.264/HEVC/VP9/AV1 NV12, H.264/HEVC/VP9 YV12, HEVC Main10/VP9 p2 P010)
- 1080p gallery streams: H.264 150/150, HEVC 150/150, VP9 150/150, AV1 150/150, HEVC10
  150/150, VP9 p2 150/150, YV12 x3 150/150
- make smoke: 6/6 codec cases; make test: PASS
- guest: 8/8 frames per codec, 0 bad buffers (10-bit ByteBuffer: VP9 p2 refused loudly,
  HEVC Main10 fails in CCodec's 8-bit converter -- open item, needs Surface output)
- 0 NVRM Xid in the window (journalctl -k, 2026-10-22 23:45 - 2026-10-23 00:10)

(cherry picked from commit 941c7b0b6a8342650f90808a67a32ece7afbcee3)
